{"availability":"available","full":"Big-Cities-Health-Coalition/use-case-catalog","name":"use-case-catalog","description":"BCHC AI Use Case Catalog — shared AI solutions from big-city health departments (GitHub Pages)","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-19T16:49:02Z","updated":"2026-10-08T17:44:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://big-cities-health-coalition.github.io/use-case-catalog/","topics":["ai","catalog","github-pages","jekyll","public-health"],"demo":"https://big-cities-health-coalition.github.io/use-case-catalog/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.110Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.110Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.110Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.110Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A shared catalog of digital tools, data projects and AI work from Big Cities Health Coalition member health departments: data pipelines, analysis code, dashboards, applications, data platforms, workflow automation, governance playbooks and AI tools. Member departments publish what they have built, the data it touches, what staffing and money it took, and what they would do differently, so another city can decide in a couple of minutes whether it is worth reusing. Sharing code is optional; every entry says plainly what another department can take away, from open-source code to a description of…","The site is hosted on GitHub Pages and managed entirely through GitHub: no server, no database, no CMS login. Jekyll builds it on GitHub Actions, and every content change flows through a GitHub issue and a pull request."],"features":["GitHub-as-CMS. Anyone can propose an entry through a web form or a GitHub issue. Automation turns the issue into a pull request with the entry already drafted — screenshots downloaded into the entry folder and all — and…","Search that reads the whole write-up. Every entry is indexed per section, so a suggestion names the section it matched in, shows the sentence around the term and links straight to that heading; related entries are…","Built for evaluation, not browsing. Cards are laid out to answer \"could my team reuse this?\" in about two seconds: a badge for what is shared (open-source code, code on request, templates or a description), a result…","Screenshots and links as first-class fields. An images field gives an entry a gallery with a keyboard-navigable lightbox and honest alt text; a links field carries labelled resources — a shared drive folder, a recorded…","Modules. Turn catalog, submit, carousel, stats, events, cohorts, resources and governance on or off independently; navigation and the home page adapt automatically, and pages under a disabled module are dropped from the…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Big-Cities-Health-Coalition/use-case-catalog/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fb4df19ce03baa0d1d94c9cac45d803768f60070b24c3478eeaa120110a8537a","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.205Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:46.205Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A shared catalog of digital tools, data projects and AI work from Big Cities Health Coalition member health departments: data pipelines, analysis code, dashboards, applications, data platforms, workflow automation, governance playbooks and AI tools. Member departments publish what they have built, the data it touches, what staffing and money it took, and what they would do differently, so another city can decide in a couple of minutes whether it is worth reusing. Sharing code is optional; every entry says plainly what another department can take away, from open-source code to a description of…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Big-Cities-Health-Coalition/use-case-catalog/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Built for evaluation, not browsing. Cards are laid out to answer \"could my team reuse this?\" in